        { "id": "recipe_jollof_rice", "type": "image", "recipeId": "jollof_rice", "recipeName": "Jollof Rice", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Jollof_rice_with_vegetable.jpg/960px-Jollof_rice_with_vegetable.jpg", "caption": "*Jollof Rice* 🌴 West African classic\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• 2 cups long-grain parboiled rice\n• 400g blended tomatoes + 2 tbsp tomato paste\n• 1 onion, 1 red bell pepper, scotch bonnet\n• 60ml vegetable oil, 2 cups chicken stock\n• Thyme, curry powder, bay leaf, salt\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Fry onions in oil, add tomato paste and blended tomato-pepper mix; cook down 10 min.\n2. Season with thyme, curry, bay leaf; add stock.\n3. Stir in washed rice, cover with foil + lid, steam on low 25–30 min.\n4. Fluff and let the base toast slightly for smoky party flavour.\n\n⏱ 45 min | 🔥 ~380 kcal | 💪 Easy", "next": "recipe_actions" },
        { "id": "recipe_egusi_soup", "type": "image", "recipeId": "egusi_soup", "recipeName": "Egusi Soup", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Egusi_soup_in_a_plate.jpg/960px-Egusi_soup_in_a_plate.jpg", "caption": "*Egusi Soup* 🌴 West African favourite\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• 2 cups ground egusi (melon seeds)\n• 300g spinach or bitterleaf\n• Assorted meat/fish, 60ml palm oil\n• 1 onion, ground crayfish, pepper, stock cubes\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Cook meat with onions and seasoning; keep the stock.\n2. Heat palm oil, fry ground egusi paste in lumps 10 min.\n3. Add stock gradually, simmer 15 min.\n4. Add crayfish, pepper, greens; simmer 5 more min.\n5. Serve with pounded yam, fufu or rice.\n\n⏱ 50 min | 🔥 ~510 kcal | 💪 Medium", "next": "recipe_actions" },
        { "id": "recipe_suya_skewers", "type": "image", "recipeId": "suya_skewers", "recipeName": "Suya Skewers", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Suya_with_pepper_sauce.jpg/960px-Suya_with_pepper_sauce.jpg", "caption": "*Suya Skewers* 🌴 West African street food\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• 500g beef sirloin, thinly sliced\n• Suya spice (yaji): ground kuli-kuli/peanut, ginger, garlic, cayenne, paprika, salt\n• Oil for brushing, onions + tomatoes to serve\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Thread beef on skewers, brush lightly with oil.\n2. Coat generously in yaji spice, rest 15 min.\n3. Grill on high heat 5–7 min per side.\n4. Dust with extra yaji; serve with sliced onions and tomatoes.\n\n⏱ 30 min | 🔥 ~340 kcal | 💪 Easy", "next": "recipe_actions" },
        { "id": "recipe_injera_tibs", "type": "image", "recipeId": "injera_tibs", "recipeName": "Injera with Tibs", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Tibs_and_Injera.jpg/960px-Tibs_and_Injera.jpg", "caption": "*Injera with Tibs* ☕ East African (Ethiopia)\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• Injera flatbread (teff sourdough)\n• 500g beef or lamb, cubed\n• 2 onions, 2 tomatoes, jalapeño\n• Niter kibbeh (spiced butter), berbere spice, rosemary\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Sear meat cubes in hot niter kibbeh.\n2. Add onions, tomatoes, jalapeño and rosemary; sauté.\n3. Season with berbere; cook until juices thicken.\n4. Serve sizzling over injera — eat with your hands!\n\n⏱ 60 min | 🔥 ~450 kcal | 💪 Medium", "next": "recipe_actions" },
        { "id": "recipe_ugali_sukuma", "type": "image", "recipeId": "ugali_sukuma", "recipeName": "Ugali with Sukuma Wiki", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/Ugali_%26_Sukuma_Wiki.jpg", "caption": "*Ugali with Sukuma Wiki* ☕ East African (Kenya)\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• 2 cups maize flour + 4 cups water\n• 1 bunch sukuma wiki (collard greens), sliced\n• 1 onion, 2 tomatoes, oil, salt\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Boil water, whisk in maize flour gradually.\n2. Stir vigorously until stiff; steam 3–4 min and mould.\n3. Fry onions, add tomatoes, then greens; cook 5 min.\n4. Serve ugali hot with the sukuma wiki alongside.\n\n⏱ 20 min | 🔥 ~290 kcal | 💪 Easy", "next": "recipe_actions" },
        { "id": "recipe_tagine_chicken", "type": "image", "recipeId": "tagine_chicken", "recipeName": "Chicken Tagine", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Chicken_Veg_Tagine_Rabat_Nov25_A7CR_08908.jpg/960px-Chicken_Veg_Tagine_Rabat_Nov25_A7CR_08908.jpg", "caption": "*Chicken Tagine* 🏜 North African (Morocco)\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• 1 whole chicken, cut up\n• 2 onions, 3 garlic cloves, preserved lemon\n• Green olives, ginger, turmeric, saffron, cinnamon\n• Olive oil, fresh coriander + parsley\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Marinate chicken in spices, garlic and herbs 30 min.\n2. Brown in olive oil in the tagine or heavy pot.\n3. Add onions and a little water; cover, simmer low 1 hour.\n4. Add olives and preserved lemon for the last 10 min.\n\n⏱ 90 min | 🔥 ~420 kcal | 💪 Medium", "next": "recipe_actions" },
        { "id": "recipe_shakshuka", "type": "image", "recipeId": "shakshuka", "recipeName": "Shakshuka", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Shakshuka_by_Calliopejen1.jpg/960px-Shakshuka_by_Calliopejen1.jpg", "caption": "*Shakshuka* 🏜 North African brunch star\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• 4–6 eggs\n• 400g crushed tomatoes, 1 red bell pepper\n• 1 onion, 3 garlic cloves\n• Cumin, paprika, harissa or chilli, olive oil, feta (optional)\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Sauté onion and pepper in olive oil; add garlic and spices.\n2. Pour in tomatoes; simmer 10 min until thick.\n3. Make wells, crack in eggs; cover and cook 5–8 min.\n4. Finish with herbs (and feta); serve with crusty bread.\n\n⏱ 25 min | 🔥 ~310 kcal | 💪 Easy", "next": "recipe_actions" },
        { "id": "recipe_fufu_ndole", "type": "image", "recipeId": "fufu_ndole", "recipeName": "Fufu with Ndolé", "link": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Ndol%C3%A9_camerounais.JPG/960px-Ndol%C3%A9_camerounais.JPG", "caption": "*Fufu with Ndolé* 🌳 Central African (Cameroon 🇨🇲)\n\n📋 *Ingredients:*\n• Ndolé (bitterleaf), washed several times\n• 250g groundnuts (peanuts), boiled and blended\n• Beef, smoked fish and/or shrimp\n• 2 onions, garlic, crayfish, palm oil\n• Fufu: cassava or plantain, pounded\n\n👨‍🍳 *Steps:*\n1. Cook meat/fish with onions and garlic; keep stock.\n2. Simmer blended groundnuts in the stock 15 min.\n3. Add washed ndolé leaves, crayfish and shrimp; cook 15 min.\n4. Fry garnish onions in oil, fold in; serve with hot fufu.\n\n⏱ 55 min | 🔥 ~490 kcal | 💪 Medium", "next": "recipe_actions" },

